{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Manageability Features"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Use these words when you need to talk about manageability features"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange written and spoken information on principles, concepts, data base objects related to query analysis, and data base engines.  Describe relational database, its concepts, and principles in spoken or written texts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level.   Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive of Modal Verbs: Can"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the <b>passive voice</b> when we want to emphasize on the action and not on the person who does it.</br>  <b>Passive voice</b> can be used with any modal verb; we are going to focus on <strong>can</strong> this time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Your database can be programmed to automatically make routine tasks in order to reducing the complexity of space, memory storage and administration"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Can</strong> shares similar uses with <b>may</b> and <b>might</b>, the latest two are more formal, and <strong>can</strong> is used to express possibility, permission or ability."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Structure</br> Subject + can be + verb in past participle + complement"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples</br><span style=\"font-style:italic;\">This jar <strong>can be opened</strong> easily</br> This item <strong>can</strong> only <strong>be bought</strong> in the online store"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Many of the manageability features can be fixed to work automatically"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Performance analysis can be easily done for any period of time in the system"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Negative Questions to Ask for Agreement"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Negative questions are used to look for confirmation and reaffirmation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't you think that Oracle Database is simply amazing?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In English, it is common to make questions in a negative form to look for the agreement of the person we are speaking"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples</br> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">A: <strong>Don't</strong> you think we should divide this work accordingly?</br> B: I think you are right."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">A: carol, <strong>didn't</strong> you go to the cinemas last night?</br>B: Yeah, I did. Why? "}, {"type": "example", "content": " It sounds a little hard at the beginning, but aren't you looking for giving them all a try?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "simplify"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something simpler"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Management of files can be simplified to rebalance the storage according to your needs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "momentarily "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in just a small amount of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We will list them below and momentarily explain their purpose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "programme"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to configure or set a program"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your database can be programmed to automatically make routine tasks in order to reducing the complexity of space."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "among"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in the middle of more than two elements"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(preposition)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can set it to activate: undo management, recovery manager, server memory management, among others."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "schedule "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to organize and set events in a specific time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It allows scheduling tasks such as statistics collection and space recovery."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "occur"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It is made of a collection of functions and procedures that lets administrators and developers to control when and where several tasks would occur."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more features of Oracle and select your favorites."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a text explaining why you like those Oracle features, use the passive of modal verbs"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the text aloud to practice pronunciation."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about Oracle features. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I recommend Oracle features. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain Oracle great features.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about Oracle. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">Don't you think that Oracle Database is simply amazing?\nDatabase administrators are in charge of creating, operating and monitoring the oracle databases. In this lesson, we are going to cover some features offered by Oracle that would help you to administer your database. We will list them below and momentarily explain their purpose.\nSelf-managing database:\nYour database can be programmed to automatically make routine tasks in order to reduce the complexity of space, memory storage, and administration. You can set it to activate undo management, recovery management, and server memory management, among others.\nMany of the manageability features can be fixed to work automatically, these are:</br></div>"}, {"time": "58000", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Automatic maintenance tasks</strong>: It allows scheduling tasks such as statistics collection and space recovery.</br><strong>Automatic storage</strong>: Management of files can be simplified to rebalance the storage according to your needs.</br>\n<strong>Automatic database diagnostic monitor</strong>: Performance analysis can be easily done for any period of time in the system; it helps to find the root of any issue as well as proposing a solution to it.\n</br>Other features of Oracle Database are:</br>\n<strong>Oracle Enterprise Manager</strong>: As a client, you can use this feature to administer the environment of the databases, the servers, the applications, and the services. It can be used even to modify and tune multiple databases.</div>"}, {"time": "116000", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>SQL Developer</strong>: It's a graphical tool designed to allow you to browse, create, edit and delete database objects. It is also useful to create and view reports.\n</br><strong>SQL Access Advisor</strong>: It is similar to the SQL tuning, but this one concentrates on schema modifications. It is ideal for organizing the indexes.\n</br><strong>Scheduler</strong>: It is made of a collection of functions and procedures that let administrators and developers control when and where several tasks would occur.\n</br>It sounds a little hard at the beginning, but aren't you looking for giving them all a try?</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le03ob09re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le03ob09re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can mention some manageability features offered by Oracle databases. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can go over some characteristics of manageability features offered for Oracle databases."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What tools or software can we use to handle and manage huge databases?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What is the most important Oracle tool? Why?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}